# Switch desktop by number: not bound in skhd — macOS owns ^1..^5 (Mission
# Control > Switch to Desktop). SIP-on, skhd's event tap would swallow the key and
# yabai's `space --focus` no-ops (no scripting addition) = dead keys that do
# nothing ^1..^5 doesn't. SIP-off (SA loaded), add
# `ctrl - N : yabai -m space --focus N` here to let yabai focus spaces directly.

# Move window to a desktop AND follow it there.
#
# yabai moves the window (public API, works with SIP on) but cannot focus a
# space — `space --focus` needs the scripting addition SIP blocks. So the helper
# posts macOS's own "Switch to Desktop N" shortcut instead (symbolichotkeys
# 118-126 = ctrl+1..9, 79/81 = ctrl+left/right).
#
# The helper exists rather than a plain `osascript ... key code N using control
# down` because skhd fires while the chord's OWN ctrl+shift is still physically
# held: without forcing the event flags, macOS sees ctrl+shift+N, matches no
# shortcut, and the view never follows. yabai/helpers/space-follow.swift calls
# CGEventSetFlags to drop the held shift. It needs no Accessibility grant of its
# own — spawned by skhd, it inherits skhd's.
#
# `&&` matters: if the target space does not exist yabai exits non-zero and the
# follow is skipped, rather than switching to nowhere.
ctrl + shift - left  : yabai -m window --space prev && /Users/karlm/Code/dotfiles/yabai/helpers/space-follow left
ctrl + shift - right : yabai -m window --space next && /Users/karlm/Code/dotfiles/yabai/helpers/space-follow right

